[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Traxler Counterattack"]
[Variation "Traxler: 5.Nxf7 Bxf2+ 6.Kxf2 Nxe4+ 7.Ke3"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,mate-threat"]
[Themes "king-hunt,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... Bc5 { The Traxler. Black ignores the threat to f7 and strikes at f2, the square only White's king protects. It is objectively risky: the engine prefers White, but White has to find accurate moves. [%cal Gc5f2] }
5. Nxf7 5... Bxf2+ { Gives up the bishop to pull the king out of its shelter. When you attack, keep attacking: there is no time for slow moves. [%cal Gc5f2] }
6. Kxf2 (6. Ke2? 6... Nd4+ { A knight check that keeps the king out in the open. } 7. Kxf2 7... Nxe4+ 8. Kg1 8... Qh4) 6... Nxe4+ { Check, and a pawn back. White's king has lost its pawn cover and Black's queen can join in at once. [%cal Ge4f2] }
7. Ke3 (7. Kf1? 7... Qh4 8. Qe1 8... Ng3+ 9. Kg1 9... Qd4+) 7... Qh4 { The key idea of the whole line: ...Qh4 whenever the king is exposed. The queen eyes f2 and g3 and ties White down. [%cal Gh4f2,Gh4g3] }
8. g3 (8. Rf1? 8... Nf6 9. d3 9... d5) (8. Qf3? 8... Nf6 9. Nxh8 9... Nd4) (8. Nxh8? 8... Qf4+ { A queen check that drives the king back, and the knight on e4 covers the squares around it. } 9. Ke2 9... Qf2+ 10. Kd3 10... Nc5+ 11. Kc3 11... Qd4#) 8... Nxg3 { Opens lines against the king and attacks the rook on h1. }
9. hxg3 (9. d3? 9... Qf4#) (9. Nxh8? 9... Qf4+ 10. Kd3 10... Qd4#) (9. Nd6+ 9... cxd6 10. hxg3 10... Qd4+ 11. Kf3 11... Qxc4) 9... Qd4+ { Check, and the queen also attacks the bishop on c4. [%cal Gd4c4] }
10. Kf3 (10. Ke2? 10... Qxc4+ 11. d3 11... Qxf7) 10... O-O { Brings the king to safety and the rook into play, while still threatening the bishop on c4. }
11. Rh4 (11. Bb3? 11... d5 12. Kg2 12... Rxf7) (11. c3? 11... Qxc4) 11... e4+ { A pawn check that also blocks the rook's line to the queen. [%cal Ge5e4] }
12. Kg2 12... Qxc4 { Takes the bishop. Material is level again and White's king is still out in the open. The engine thinks this is roughly equal, which is the best result Black can hope for. } *
